<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Kuban-Black Sea Soviet Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1918 CE · capital Yekaterinodar</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Soviet republic formed in May 1918 by merging the Kuban and Black Sea soviets during the Russian Civil War.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 28 May 1918 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-the-soviet-union">Bolsheviks</a> united the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kuban-soviet-republic">Kuban Soviet Republic</a>, centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krasnodar">Yekaterinodar</a>, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/black-sea-soviet-republic">Black Sea Soviet Republic</a>, based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/novorossiysk">Novorossiysk</a>, into a single Kuban-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> Soviet Republic, as an autonomous part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Russian SFSR</a>. The merger reflected the threat posed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volunteer-army">Volunteer Army</a> and by German forces advancing from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic was governed by a council of commissars and fought both the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volunteer-army">Volunteer Army</a> and the Kuban <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> government. In June 1918, on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladimir-lenin">Lenin</a>'s orders, much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea-fleet">Black Sea Fleet</a> was scuttled in the bay of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/novorossiysk">Novorossiysk</a> to prevent its capture by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. The republic struggled with grain requisitions and Cossack resistance.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In July 1918 it was merged with the Terek and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stavropol">Stavropol</a> soviet republics into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/north-caucasian-soviet-republic">North Caucasian Soviet Republic</a>, which the White armies overran by the end of the year.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kuban-black-sea-soviet-republic.jpg" alt="Kuban-Black Sea Soviet Republic" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: User:R-41 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Socialist_red_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Yekaterinodar</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Russia</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kuban-Black Sea SR</dd></dl></aside></div>
